    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="0262" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg250"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860C.20/84: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-08-25T19:00:00+03:00">August 25, 1941—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 25—5:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1576. My 1520, August 16, 6 p.m. General Anders told me yesterday that he has
                    already succeeded in organizing 2 divisions of Poles and that he expects to be
                    able to organize 2 more in the near future and ultimately to raise the total
                    number to 6.</p>
                <p>He said the Soviet authorities are providing the arms for the 2 divisions already
                    organized including field artillery, but neither tanks nor airplanes, but had
                    informed him that it would be necessary for him to obtain all of the arms for
                    any additional troops from Great Britain or the United States. The General added
                    that he had received assurances from the British that uniforms for 50,000 men
                    would be forthcoming as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
